# VisionForge — Git Flow & Linear

**GitHub:** https://github.com/dawarazhar11/VisionForge  
**Linear:** VisionForge project (team: Dawar-personal)

## Git flow

```
master  ← production (GitHub default)
  ↑
develop ← integration branch
  ↑
feature/daw-XX-short-name
```

1. Start from `develop`: `git checkout develop && git pull origin develop`
2. Create branch: `git checkout -b feature/daw-37-wire-models-api`
3. Commit format: `type(scope): message (DAW-XX)` — e.g. `feat(flutter): wire ModelsScreen (DAW-37)`
4. Push: `git push -u origin feature/daw-XX-short-name`
5. Open PR on GitHub: **feature → develop**
6. At milestone completion: PR **develop → master**

Never commit directly to `master`. Never force-push `master`.

## Linear (every dev session)

**Starting work**
- Set issue status to **In Progress**
- Branch name must include Linear ID (`feature/daw-37-...`)

**Finishing work**
- Mark issue **Done** after PR merges to `develop`
- Add comment with GitHub PR URL + merge commit SHA
- If a feature batch closes a milestone, create a `[Done summary]` issue listing delivered items and PR links

**Already shipped** — baseline DAW-93–99, plus DAW-36–39, DAW-76 (Flutter/API wiring) and DAW-119 (generic .blend render pipeline). See Done issues in Linear.

